    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">Dear colleague,</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">A final reminder that our webinar, <strong>Strengthening the Electoral Profession: How to Improve Knowledge Sharing</strong>, takes place <strong>this Thursday, 4 June at 14:00 UTC</strong>. If you have not yet registered, there is still time to join us.</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">Electoral bodies build extraordinary institutional knowledge through every cycle, yet much of it stays locked within institutions or disappears when staff move on. This session asks what a practical improvement actually looks like, with three contributors:</p>

    <!-- Speaker 1 -->
    <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="margin: 0 0 12px; background-color:#f0f4f8; border-radius:6px;">
    <tr><td style="padding: 14px 20px;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 2px; color:#1a2744; font-size:14px; font-weight:700;">Sy Mamabolo</p>
        <p style="margin:0; color:#555; font-size:13px; line-height:1.5;">Chief Electoral Officer, Electoral Commission of South Africa (IEC), on the current picture.</p>
    </td></tr>
    </table>

    <!-- Speaker 2 -->
    <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="margin: 0 0 12px; background-color:#f0f4f8; border-radius:6px;">
    <tr><td style="padding: 14px 20px;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 2px; color:#1a2744; font-size:14px; font-weight:700;">Tammy Patrick</p>
        <p style="margin:0; color:#555; font-size:13px; line-height:1.5;">CEO for Programs, Election Center (US National Association of Election Officials), on the international view and professional credentialling.</p>
    </td></tr>
    </table>

    <!-- Speaker 3 -->
    <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="margin: 0 0 24px; background-color:#f0f4f8; border-radius:6px;">
